KG42.register("clusters-e2571404c17db9b8ae589a1e",{"id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v142-d-K004","paper":"18-dlmp_analysis","label":"Conditional linkage between radial distribution-network welfare allocation and active-power DLMP","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"Conditional linkage between radial distribution-network welfare allocation and active-power DLMP","market_meaning":"Taking generation/consumption benefits and costs, network constraints and equipment capabilities as inputs, welfare optimization, allocation feasibility and the interpretation of nodal active-power DLMP are presented jointly. The implicit-function model (I), the SOCP model (II) and network-loss pricing under a single marginal resource each retain their own conditions; the existing Rule-Chain does not yet constitute a closed joint computational model.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M03"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"The three Rule-Chains share the network and economic-quantity definitions of M03, which suffices to establish an interface among objective, constraints and price interpretation. However, the variable roles, shunt terms and root-node voltage ranges of models (I)/(II) differ, and the perturbation sign of Proposition 3 is not sufficiently bound; the feasible regions or resulting prices cannot be directly deemed generally equivalent.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Feasible constraints determine the allowable range of welfare allocation, and the price Rule-Chain interprets the nodal marginal value of that optimization, giving a clear information-decision linkage. These Rule-Chains are presented together while retaining both models and the single-marginal-resource condition, avoiding counting summaries of different functions repeatedly as independent rules or combining them into an unsupported new model.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide allocation feasibility, the mathematical constraints of the main model (I) and the physical-interpretation conditions of model (II)."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the welfare objective and the constraint scope of the two models, linking allocation and price interpretation; unformalized content remains as is."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide active-power balance multiplier pricing, the generator interior-point condition and the network-loss price relationship under a single marginal resource, each retaining its applicable conditions."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C004","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C005","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C006","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C007","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C008","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C009"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E016","v141-b-g01-E017","v141-b-g01-E018"],"rationale":"The source explicitly pairs the welfare objective of model (I) with the feasible constraints (2)-(15). R009 provides constraint details, and R010 provides the objective and scope; this mapping does not supply a missing objective object."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C010"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023"],"rationale":"The equality condition in R009 supplements the scope of physical interpretation of the SOCP solution in R010. It is not an unconditional equality in the original relaxation, nor can it replace the other constraints of model (II)."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E020","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E024","v141-b-g03-E04"],"rationale":"The welfare optimization of model (II) contains nodal active-power balance, and the source directly interprets its multiplier as the nodal active-power DLMP, supporting the optimization-pricing interface; the complete primal-dual binding still awaits upstream supplementation."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-pig","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Pgplus","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Pgminus"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x-p-i-g","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-theta-P-i-g-plus","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-theta-P-i-g-minus","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e12"],"rationale":"The generation output and its upper and lower bounds under the same definition both constrain the allocation and are used to determine whether the generator in model (II) is strictly in the interior; price equals marginal cost only under that condition."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C008","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-li","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-R"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x-l-i","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-theta-R-i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E017","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"],"rationale":"The proof of Proposition 3 uses total active-power balance and the same branch loss quantity, forming an interface between allocation and marginal-loss price interpretation; the single-marginal-resource condition is retained, and the perturbation sign and cross-model balance differences are listed as unresolved items."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R011::V::clearing.social_welfare"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R010::V::clearing.social_welfare","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E020","v141-b-g02-e15"],"rationale":"Both references point to the M03 welfare-optimization function, used respectively for objective description and marginal-price interpretation. Only the function display is unified; the model conditions remain in the original Rule-Chains."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O002","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E018"],"rationale":"Both summarize the same set of line, capacity, voltage and balance constraints of model (I), with the same scope of application. The representative covers only this feasibility summary, not the welfare objective of R010 or the content of model (II)."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O003","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E023"],"rationale":"Both procedural constraints represent the equality condition (20) required for model (II) to obtain physical interpretation, with the same condition and scope; they are not merged with the unconditional relaxation constraint."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-pig","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x-p-i-g"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E013"],"rationale":"The same M03 node definition and capacity constraints confirm that both are nodal active-power generation. Their different local uses in allocation feasibility and price interior-point determination are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-pic","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x-p-i-c"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E014"],"rationale":"Both are active-power consumption at non-root nodes in M03, with the same definition and index range; the respective uses of the Rule-Chains in feasible allocation and price derivation are retained separately, and on that basis they are not deemed equal to the perturbation D_n."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-li","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x-l-i"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g02-e14"],"rationale":"The two correspond to the squared current magnitude of the same branch. R009 distinguishes the implicit function of model (I) and the decision quantity of model (II), and R011 is used for loss sensitivity; only the physical quantity is associated, without rewriting the local role or domain."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Pgplus","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-theta-P-i-g-plus"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E013"],"rationale":"The common definition confirms that both are the active-power generation capacity upper bound of the same node, used respectively for feasibility and strict interior-point determination; the original parameter records, whose numerical values are not given, are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O008","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Pgminus","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-theta-P-i-g-minus"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E013"],"rationale":"The common definition confirms that both are the active-power generation capacity lower bound of the same node, used respectively for feasibility and strict interior-point determination; the two parameter records are not folded into a new object."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O009","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-R","v141-c-R011::theta::v141-c-R011-theta-R-i"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g02-e14"],"rationale":"The same branch definition and loss definition confirm that both are branch resistance; their different uses in line constraints, total balance and price sensitivity are retained."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R010 does not formalize an objective, variables or parameters. R009 mainly provides the feasible constraints of model (I) and the tightness conditions of model (II), and cannot replace the voltage-drop, nodal-balance and complete relaxation constraints of model (II); the multiplier pricing in R011 still lacks a complete primal-dual binding.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C010","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E020","v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E024"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Within the same M03 scope, C should supplement the complete objective, model constraints and object bindings for benefits, shunt terms, tree topology and multipliers, while retaining the distinction between the two models; D does not fabricate these scientific objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G002","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The total balance of model (I) explicitly lists only branch losses, whereas the nodal balance of model (II) also contains shunt conductance and susceptance terms; the voltage constraints of model (I) cover N^+, while model (II) includes the root node. Therefore, solely because quantity definitions are shared, they cannot be regarded as having the same feasible region or as guaranteeing consistent prices.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C007","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C008","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C009","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E016","v141-b-g01-E017","v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E022"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the shunt terms and root-node boundary assumptions of the two models and clarify the comparable scope; if equivalence is to be claimed, source-supported conditions or proofs should be added, otherwise the models continue to be retained as different models."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G003","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The equality condition required for physical interpretation does not mean that all SOCP optimal solutions satisfy that condition. The exactness statement of E023 is restricted to infinite upper bounds on active- and reactive-power consumption at non-root nodes and guarantees only the existence of an optimal solution satisfying the equality; these restrictions have not yet entered the frozen Rule-Chain as complete conditions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C010","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Pcplus","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-Qcplus","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E023"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should verify and record the exactness conditions and existential quantifier, and clarify whether a given solution satisfies tightness; under finite consumption upper bounds, the stated guarantee must not be applied directly."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G004","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R009-C010 uses a representation divided by l_i, while the frozen definition of l_i allows non-negative values, and the existing content does not explain the expression's interpretation at zero current. On that basis, the formula cannot be regarded as closed over the entire recorded domain.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-li","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C010"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E023"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the domain of validity or zero-current convention in the source, and have C record it explicitly; strict positivity conditions must not be added on one's own in D, nor may the frozen expression be replaced."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G005","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"Proposition 3 calls D_n net injection, but the total balance in the proof and the substituted objective do not explicitly give the location of that perturbation, and state that the derivatives of other generation/consumption quantities are zero. The current binding is insufficient to verify the constant terms and perturbation direction of (68)/(71), and also insufficient to map D_n directly to p_n^c or the net-injection vector.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C008","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001","v141-c-R011::x::v141-c-R011-x-p-i-c","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E017","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e12"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the positive/negative direction of D_n, the independent perturbation location and the loss-derivative definition, and have C supplement the object binding between price and perturbation; retain the single marginal resource and related interior-point conditions, and do not change the sign in the frozen formula without basis."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G006","category":"unverified_source","description":"The models, conditions and price derivations of this Rule-Cluster are all based on candidate evidence that remains unverified; the B transcription and downstream mathematics have not undergone the independent review omitted by this experiment.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E017","v141-b-g01-E020","v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g01-E022","v141-b-g01-E023","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g03-E04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently, manually check the source, indices, symbols and conditions formula by formula, and inspect all assembly mappings; the availability of candidate evidence does not mean that the source or scientific conclusions have been approved."}]},"rule_refs":["18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R009","18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R010","18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R011"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-851574b724899235","COMP-da9b2e714c674f55","COMP-ebacec241379c91d"]});
